; Assembler.0.6
; This update is implementing the changes brought up in the previous updates into the assembler.
; Moving Strings to the DATA section To optimze the size of the binary and the efficiency of the `main` function.
; I will also change the strings to be null terminated instead of printing by length.
; This means changing `print_string(ptr, length)` to `print_string(ptr)`.
; This function will print characters until it reaches the `\0` character.
; Currently when encoding a uleb number, if the input is not 0-9 there is no error warning, and it will crash at runtime.
; To fix this, in the `writeFromUleb`, check to make sure the input is within the digits 0-9.
; There are a few times in the code when trying to encde a specific value that the limitations of uleb encoding occur.
; This happens when the value was expected to be in SLEB 128 format. For example in the code:
;
; ```
; i32.const sleb 128
; i32.const sleb 52
; i32.sub
; ```
;
; could be shortened to:
;
; ```
; i32.const sleb 76
; ```
;
; To encode the correct number.

; Imports Changed:
; print_string(ptr, len) -> print_string(ptr)
; The host will also have to update this change on its end.

; code below:

; Global memory addresses (i32.load reads values; i32.store changes them).
#sectionMemory 4194304
#functionMemory 5242880
#symbol_names 6291456
#symbol_values 6307840

; Mutable global values occupy one four-byte slot each.
#SECTION_BYTES_OUT 6324224
#SECTION_LAST_BYTES_OUT 6324228
#FUNCTION_BYTES_OUT 6324232
#FUNCTION_LAST_BYTES_OUT 6324236
#WRITING_TO_FUNCTION 6324240
